--TEST--
Assigning to a variable that was never declared is `E0301`, and its label and help say in plain words how to declare it, with a type or with `var`
--FILE--
<?nvs
$count = 3;
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0301]: `$count` is assigned to but was never declared
  --> case.nvs:2:1
  |
2 | $count = 3;
  | ^^^^^^ this variable has no declaration
  = help: declare `$count` with its type or with `var` the first time you assign it, such as `var $count = ...;`
%A
